ve-support vote causality, uniform timers and network fast-path remain separate limits rather than assumptions about this API outcome.\"\n      ],\n      \"understanding\": \"unchanged\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Continue the same accepted Candidate and F-verify-support lifecycle because the proposition is unchanged. This check replaces assigned-state and isolated-fragment risks with one real history per scenario. Keep the other frontier surfaces deferred until this bounded public endpoint is executed and reviewed.\",\n      \"question_updates\": {}\n    }\n  }\n]\ncurrent {\n  \"phase\": \"executed\",\n  \"operation_id\": \"f0fd7479adcd418884ccfb446842e310\",\n  \"action\": \"check\",\n  \"direct_check_id\": \"318065aead82494797d283e378195a4e\"\n}\nunits [\n  {\n    \"id\": \"unit-O-verify-current-authority\",\n    \"candidate_id\": \"e882dd28e3a74f959e62c629f3382252\",\n    \"obligation_ids\": [\n      \"O-verify-current-authority\"\n    ],\n    \"binding_ids\": [\n      \"L-verify-api\",\n      \"L-verify-registration\",\n      \"L-verify-count\",\n      \"L-verify-completion\"\n    ],\n    \"relation_ids\": [],\n    \"scope\": {\n      \"description\": \"Public VerifyLeader authority assurance in a crash-free protocol-v3 cluster with stable voter/nonvoter membership, under transport partitions. A replacement leader and its successful command completion precede the verification call. The old peer has no voter-majority communication or subsequent authority acquisition during the invocation.\",\n      \"assumptions\": [\n        \"Distinct permanent ServerIDs and unchanged valid membership during the observed partition\",\n        \"Honest actual Raft workers and request/response transports; dropped routes produce errors, never fabricated success\",\n        \"Independent validated node-local timeouts; no crashes or storage loss in this execution\"\n      ],\n      \"excluded\": [\n        \"Log-commit agreement or full read linearizability proof\",\n        \"Membership transitions during verification\",\n        \"Crashes, partial storage writes, user restore and mixed protocol versions\",\n        \"Any liveness guarantee from tool deadlines\"\n      ],\n      \"parameters\": {\n        \"protocol_version\": 3\n      }\n    },\n    \"rationale\": \"Derive the obligation from the public leadership assurance, with actual higher-term election and completed write as its antecedent. The selected Fact and direct roles are unchanged.\",\n    \"status\": \"partial\",\n    \"previous_id\": null,\n    \"version\": 1,\n    \"boundary_changes\": [],\n    \"obligation_checks\": {\n      \"O-verify-current-authority\": [\n        \"bcaed4ce26bf44d797a18ec78b37a154\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"remaining_obligation_ids\": [\n      \"O-verify-current-authority\"\n    ],\n    \"recheck_reasons\": [],\n    \"semantic_readiness\": {},\n    \"coverage_limitations\": [\n      \"Bounded direct comparison completed; local attribution remains pending: Direct oracle correspondence is unreviewed\"\n    ],\n    \"record\": {\n      \"path\": \"state.json\",\n      \"collection\": \"units\",\n      \"match\": {\n        \"id\": \"unit-O-verify-current-authority\",\n        \"version\": 1\n      }\n    }\n  }\n]\nclaims [\n  {\n    \"id\": \"O-verify-current-authority\",\n    \"kind\": \"obligation\",\n    \"concern\": \"implementation_semantics\",\n    \"description\": \"When a different peer has already acquired leadership in a higher term and completed a command before a VerifyLeader invocation, the former leader must not complete that invocation successfully while it remains separated from the voting quorum and has not reacquired authority. Positive support from replication participants cannot make this obsolete authority assurance successful.\",\n    \"scope\": {\n      \"description\": \"Public VerifyLeader authority assurance in a crash-free protocol-v3 cluster with stable voter/nonvoter membership, under transport partitions. A replacement leader and its successful command completion precede the verification call. The old peer has no voter-majority communication or subsequent authority acquisition during the invocation.\",\n      \"assumptions\": [\n        \"Distinct permanent ServerIDs and unchanged valid membership during the observed partition\",\n        \"Honest actual Raft workers and request/response transports; dropped routes produce errors, never fabricated success\",\n        \"Independent validated node-local timeouts; no crashes or storage loss in this execution\"\n      ],\n      \"excluded\": [\n        \"Log-commit agreement or full read linearizability proof\",\n        \"Membership transitions during verification\",\n        \"Crashes, partial storage writes, user restore and mixed protocol versions\",\n        \"Any liveness guarantee from tool deadlines\"\n      ],\n      \"parameters\": {\n        \"protocol_version\": 3\n      }\n    },\n    \"source\": \"Candidate derived from attributed implementation responsibilities\",\n    \"source_ids\": [\n      \"S-api-verify\",\n      \"S-membership-contract\",\n      \"S-vote-producer\",\n      \"S-election\",\n      \"S-verify-existing-tests\"\n    ],\n    \"pending\": [],\n    \"assessment\": \"unassessed\",\n    \"candidate\": true,\n    \"grounding\": {\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"S-api-verify\",\n        \"S-membership-contract\",\n        \"S-vote-producer\",\n        \"S-election\",\n        \"S-verify-existing-tests\"\n      ],\n      \"expectation_ids\": [\n        \"S-api-verify\"\n      ],\n      \"binding_ids\": [\n        \"L-verify-api\",\n        \"L-verify-registration\",\n        \"L-verify-count\",\n        \"L-verify-completion\"\n      ],\n      \"derivation\": \"The public API explicitly says VerifyLeader ensures this peer is still the leader and can prevent stale FSM data after leadership loss. A completed operation on a different, higher-term elected leader before invocation fixes the temporal countercondition: the former peer cannot place a successful assurance before the replacement event. Voter membership governs real election grants and tally; replicated nonvoters cannot supply an alternative authority acquisition. This requirement is derived from that public assurance, not from insisting that the code use a particular quorum algorithm. Existing tests provide narrower expectations for healthy and lost-leader cases, not proof of this history.\",\n      \"applicability\": \"The fixed membership and bidirectional cut prevent the old peer from reacquiring elected authority during the call. Nonuniform timeouts change the size of the observation interval but do not waive the public API condition. Failure or a pending verification is allowed; no positive liveness obligation is introduced.\",\n      \"unresolved\": [],\n      \"conflicts\": [],\n      \"alternatives\": [\n        \"Lease expiration, negative replies or received newer-term requests may correctly cause verification to fail. No specific failing error string is required.\",\n        \"A genuinely reacquired authority context would invalidate the antecedent, but the submitted cut excludes that path.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"version\": 1,\n    \"record\": {\n      \"path\": \"state.json\",\n      \"collection\": \"claims\",\n      \"match\": {\n        \"id\": \"O-verify-current-authority\",\n        \"version\": 1\n      }\n    }\n  }\n]\nartifacts [\n  {\n    \"id\": \"318065aead82494797d283e378195a4e\",\n    \"version\": 1,\n    \"plan_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-09-29_11-09-41-hashicorp_raft-real-run/direct-checks/f0fd7479adcd418884ccfb446842e310/plan.json\",\n    \"harness_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-09-29_11-09-41-hashicorp_raft-real-run/direct-checks/f0fd7479adcd418884ccfb446842e310/assurance_generated_test.go\",\n    \"unit_id\": \"unit-O-verify-current-authority\",\n    \"claim_id\": \"O-verify-current-authority\",\n    \"graph_versions\": {\n  