rove the exact cause.\"\n  ],\n  \"reviewed_complete\": false,\n  \"bounded_complete\": true,\n  \"confirmed\": false,\n  \"outcome\": \"violated\",\n  \"level\": \"implementation_test\",\n  \"claim_id\": \"O-verify-current-authority\",\n  \"claim_version\": 1,\n  \"framework_revision\": \"audit-products-v30\",\n  \"finding_ids\": {\n    \"P-no-obsolete-verification\": \"7b1f3c3efff34ad3b2a9dbdfd921a146\"\n  },\n  \"finding_id\": \"7b1f3c3efff34ad3b2a9dbdfd921a146\"\n}\nbindings {\n  \"associations\": [\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"O-verify-current-authority\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"S-api-verify\",\n        \"S-api-verify\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Public invocation creates a verifyFuture and queues it; the harness observes that actual future Error return, not role polling as a substitute for success.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"anchor\": {\n    \"source_ids\": [\n      \"S-api-verify\"\n    ],\n    \"boundary_complete\": true,\n    \"kind\": \"declaration\",\n    \"material_id\": \"S-api-verify\",\n    \"start_line\": 883,\n    \"end_line\": 883,\n    \"symbol\": \"Raft.VerifyLeader\"\n  },\n  \"material_id\": \"S-api-verify\",\n  \"id\": \"L-verify-api\",\n  \"file\": \"api.go\",\n  \"symbol\": \"Raft.VerifyLeader\",\n  \"start_line\": 883,\n  \"end_line\": 893,\n  \"snapshot_id\": \"5a56266f5e5e42b38ae94f6b06a2fda3\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"499a72c01096912e85d16381f4640ac6d29f8c2b91cabbdae8530bdcbeb89a4a\",\n  \"basis\": \"agent_inference\",\n  \"description\": \"Public invocation creates a verifyFuture and queues it; the harness observes that actual future Error return, not role polling as a substitute for success.\",\n  \"pending\": [],\n  \"excerpt\": \"func (r *Raft) VerifyLeader() Future {\\n\\tmetrics.IncrCounter([]string{\\\"raft\\\", \\\"verify_leader\\\"}, 1)\\n\\tverifyFuture := &verifyFuture{}\\n\\tverifyFuture.init()\\n\\tselect {\\n\\tcase <-r.shutdownCh:\\n\\t\\treturn errorFuture{ErrRaftShutdown}\\n\\tcase r.verifyCh <- verifyFuture:\\n\\t\\treturn verifyFuture\\n\\t}\\n}\",\n  \"version\": 1\n}\nbindings {\n  \"associations\": [\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"O-verify-current-authority\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"S-verify-register\",\n        \"S-api-verify\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Captures voter-derived threshold but registers with every replication worker; this is the direct context for consumption of F-verify-support.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"anchor\": {\n    \"source_ids\": [\n      \"S-verify-register\"\n    ],\n    \"boundary_complete\": true,\n    \"kind\": \"declaration\",\n    \"material_id\": \"S-verify-register\",\n    \"start_line\": 965,\n    \"end_line\": 965,\n    \"symbol\": \"Raft.verifyLeader\"\n  },\n  \"material_id\": \"S-verify-register\",\n  \"id\": \"L-verify-registration\",\n  \"file\": \"raft.go\",\n  \"symbol\": \"Raft.verifyLeader\",\n  \"start_line\": 965,\n  \"end_line\": 987,\n  \"snapshot_id\": \"5a56266f5e5e42b38ae94f6b06a2fda3\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"54d43df5197fd71cd0f6ae4eee1ba28efb139a5223eb14b756c606bdb0b8a800\",\n  \"basis\": \"agent_inference\",\n  \"description\": \"Captures voter-derived threshold but registers with every replication worker; this is the direct context for consumption of F-verify-support.\",\n  \"pending\": [],\n  \"excerpt\": \"func (r *Raft) verifyLeader(v *verifyFuture) {\\n\\t// Current leader always votes for self\\n\\tv.votes = 1\\n\\n\\t// Set the quorum size, hot-path for single node\\n\\tv.quorumSize = r.quorumSize()\\n\\tif v.quorumSize == 1 {\\n\\t\\tv.respond(nil)\\n\\t\\treturn\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\t// Track this request\\n\\tv.notifyCh = r.verifyCh\\n\\tr.leaderState.notify[v] = struct{}{}\\n\\n\\t// Trigger immediate heartbeats\\n\\tfor _, repl := range r.leaderState.replState {\\n\\t\\trepl.notifyLock.Lock()\\n\\t\\trepl.notify[v] = struct{}{}\\n\\t\\trepl.notifyLock.Unlock()\\n\\t\\tasyncNotifyCh(repl.notifyCh)\\n\\t}\\n}\",\n  \"version\": 1\n}\nbindings {\n  \"associations\": [\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"O-verify-current-authority\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"S-verify-vote\",\n        \"S-api-verify\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Consumes boolean worker support into a scalar threshold and asynchronously notifies the main loop; peer voter identity is not rechecked here.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"anchor\": {\n    \"source_ids\": [\n      \"S-verify-vote\"\n    ],\n    \"boundary_complete\": true,\n    \"kind\": \"declaration\",\n    \"material_id\": \"S-verify-vote\",\n    \"start_line\": 274,\n    \"end_line\": 274,\n    \"symbol\": \"verifyFuture.vote\"\n  },\n  \"material_id\": \"S-verify-vote\",\n  \"id\": \"L-verify-count\",\n  \"file\": \"future.go\",\n  \"symbol\": \"verifyFuture.vote\",\n  \"start_line\": 274,\n  \"end_line\": 293,\n  \"snapshot_id\": \"5a56266f5e5e42b38ae94f6b06a2fda3\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"e3775d16c6cb24f9c9572ce452c27e87fcbf4b24baf666d14e838cc4b571ae9c\",\n  \"basis\": \"agent_inference\",\n  \"description\": \"Consumes boolean worker support into a scalar threshold and asynchronously notifies the main loop; peer voter identity is not rechecked here.\",\n  \"pending\": [],\n  \"excerpt\": \"func (v *verifyFuture) vote(leader bool) {\\n\\tv.voteLock.Lock()\\n\\tdefer v.voteLock.Unlock()\\n\\n\\t// Guard against having notified already\\n\\tif v.notifyCh == nil {\\n\\t\\treturn\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tif leader {\\n\\t\\tv.votes++\\n\\t\\tif v.votes >= v.quorumSize {\\n\\t\\t\\tv.notifyCh <- v\\n\\t\\t\\tv.notifyCh = nil\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t} else {\\n\\t\\tv.notifyCh <- v\\n\\t\\tv.notifyCh = nil\\n\\t}\\n}\",\n  \"version\": 1\n}\nbindings {\n  \"associations\": [\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"O-verify-current-authority\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"S-leader-loop\",\n        \"S-api-verify\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Main loop returns nil after sufficient counted support or errors after negative verification. This actual public-completion branch is where obsolete support could violate the assurance.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"anchor\": {\n    \"source_ids\": [\n      \"S-leader-loop\"\n    ],\n    \"boundary_complete\": true,\n    \"kind\": \"declaration\",\n    \"material_id\": \"S-leader-loop\",\n    \"start_line\": 667,\n    \"end_line\": 667,\n    \"symbol\": \"Raft.leaderLoop\"\n  },\n  \"material_id\": \"S-leader-loop\",\n  \"id\": \"L-verify-completion\",\n  \"file\": \"raft.go\",\n  \"symbol\": \"Raft.leaderLoop\",\n  \"start_line\": 848,\n  \"end_line\": 870,\n  \"snapshot_id\": \"5a56266f5e5e42b38ae94f6b06a2fda3\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"54d43df5197fd71cd0f6ae4eee1ba28efb139a5223eb14b756c606bdb0b8a800\",\n  \"basis\": \"agent_inference\",\n  \"description\": \"Main loop returns nil after sufficient counted support or errors after negative verification. This actual public-completion branch is where obsolete support could violate the assurance.\",\n  \"pending\": [],\n  \"excerpt\": \"\\t\\tcase v := <-r.verifyCh:\\n\\t\\t\\tr.mainThreadSaturation.working()\\n\\t\\t\\tif v.quorumSize == 0 {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t// Just dispatched, start the verification\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tr.verifyLeader(v)\\n\\t\\t\\t} else if v.votes < v.quorumSize {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t// Early return, means there must be a new leader\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tr.logger.Warn(\\\"new leader elected, stepping down\\\")\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tr.setState(Follower)\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tdelete(r.leaderState.notify, v)\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tfor _, repl := range r.leaderState.replState {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\trepl.cleanNotify(v)\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tv.respond(ErrNotLeader)\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t} else {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t// Quorum of members agree, we are still leader\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tdelete(r.leaderState.notify, v)\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tfor _, repl := range r.leaderState.replState {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\trepl.cleanNotify(v)\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tv.respond(nil)\\n\\t\\t\\t}\",\n  \"version\": 1\n}\nFIXED PLAN {\n  \"description\": \"Replace the accepted candidate's prefix, producer and public-endpoint gaps using real four-node histories. Compare old VerifyLeader after a newer leader completes a command with and without connectivity to the nonvoter. Observe completed futures and raw FSM values; the controller applies an independent no-success-after-supersession oracle.\",\n  \"claim_id\": \"O-verify-current-authority\",\n  \"binding_ids\": [\n    \"L-verify-api\",\n    \"L-verify-registration\",\n    \"L-verify-count\",\n    \"L-verify-completion\"\n  ],\n  \"harness\": {\n    \"files\": {},\n    \"kind\": \"go_test\",\n    \"source\": \"package raft\\n\\nimport (\\n    \\\"encoding/json\\\"\\n    \\\"fmt\\\"\\n    \\\"io\\\"\\n    \\\"sync\\\"\\n    \\\"testing\\\"\\n    \\\"time\\\"\\n)\\n\\n// The transport retains the real in-memory RPC producer/receiver paths. The\\n// optional pipeline is disabled so a partition cuts the same routes for every\\n// AppendEntries call; successful responses are never synthesized.\\ntype assuranceTransport struct {\\n    *InmemTransport\\n    mu sync.Mutex\\n    replies map[ServerID]int\\n}\\n\\nfunc (a *assuranceTransport) AppendEntriesPipeline(id ServerID, addr ServerAddress) (AppendPipeline, error) {\\n    return nil, ErrPipelineReplicationNotSupported\\n}\\n\\nfunc (a *assuranceTransport) AppendEntries(id ServerID, addr ServerAddress, req *AppendEntriesRequest, resp *AppendEntriesResponse) error {\\n    err := a.InmemTransport.AppendEntries(id, addr, req, resp)\\n    if err == nil && resp.Success {\\n        a.mu.Lock()\\n        a.replies[id]++\\n        a.mu.Unlock()\\n    }\\n    return err\\n}\\n\\nfunc (a *assuranceTransport) counts() map[string]int {\\n    a.mu.Lock()\\n    defer a.mu.Unlock()\\n    c := make(map[string]int)\\n    for k, v := range a.replies { c[string(k)] = v }\\n    return c\\n}\\n\\ntype assuranceNode struct {\\n    r *Raft\\n    tr *assuranceTransport\\n    fsm *MockFSM\\n    id ServerID\\n    addr ServerAddress\\n}\\n\\nfunc assuranceEmit(event string, fields map[string]interface{}) {\\n    fields[\\\"event\\\"] = event\\n    b, err := json.Marshal(fields)\\n    if err != nil { panic(err) }\\n    fmt.Println(\\\"CA_EVENT \\\" + string(b))\\n}\\n\\nfunc assuranceAwait(t *testing.T, f Future, d time.Duration) error {\\n    t.Helper()\\n    ch := make(chan error, 1)\\n    go func() { ch <- f.Error() }()\\n    select {\\n    case err := <-ch: return err\\n    case <-time.After(d): t.Fatal(\\\"future completion deadline: observation is incomplete\\\"); return nil\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfunc assuranceUntil(t *testing.T, d time.Duration, what string, pred func() bool) {\\n    t.Helper()\\n    stop := time.Now().Add(d)\\n    for time.Now().Before(stop) {\\n        if pred() { return }\\n        time.Sleep(2*time.Millisecond)\\n    }\\n    t.Fatalf(\\\"unreached prerequisite: %s\\\", what)\\n}\\n\\nfunc assuranceLast(n *assuranceNode) string {\\n    n.fsm.Lock()\\n    defer n.fsm.Unlock()\\n    if len(n.fsm.logs)==0 { return \\\"\\\" }\\n    return string(n.fsm.logs[len(n.fsm.logs)-1])\\n}\\n\\nfunc TestAssuranceVerifyAuthorityHistory(t *testing.T) {\\n    for _, keepNonvoter := range []bool{true, false} {\\n        name := \\\"with_nonvoter\\\"\\n        if !keepNonvoter { name = \\\"without_nonvoter_contact\\\" }\\n        t.Run(name, func(t *testing.T) {\\n            nodes := make([]*assuranceNode, 4)\\n            for i := range nodes {\\n                id := ServerID(fmt.Sprintf(\\\"%s_node_%d\\\", name, i))\\n                addr, base := NewInmemTransportWithTimeout(ServerAddress(id), 40*time.Millisecond)\\n                nodes[i] = &assuranceNode{id:id, addr:addr, tr:&assuranceTransport{InmemTransport:base, replies:make(map[ServerID]int)}, fsm:&MockFSM{}}\\n            }\\n            for i,n := range nodes {\\n                for j,p := range nodes {\\n                    if i!=j { n.tr.Connect(p.addr, p.tr.InmemTransport) }\\n                }\\n            }\\n            defer func() {\\n                // Initiate shutdown for all nodes before waiting for any one.\\n                var fs []Future\\n                for _,n := range nodes { if n.r!=nil { fs=append(fs,n.r.Shutdown()) } }\\n                for _,n := range nodes { n.tr.Close() }\\n                for _,f := range fs { assuranceAwait(t,f,3*time.Second) }\\n            }()\\n            for i,n := range nodes {\\n                cfg := DefaultConfig()\\n                cfg.ProtocolVersion = 3\\n                cfg.LocalID = n.id\\n                cfg.LogOutput = io.Discard\\n                cfg.CommitTimeout = 5*time.Millisecond\\n                cfg.HeartbeatTimeout = 100*time.Millisecond\\n                cfg.ElectionTimeout = 150*time.Millisecond\\n                cfg.LeaderLeaseTimeout = 80*time.Millisecond\\n                if i==0 {\\n                    // A longer local lease leaves an observable interval after\\n                    // the remote voters elect. All safety/lease workers still run.\\n                    cfg.HeartbeatTimeout = 2*time.Second\\n                    cfg.ElectionTimeout = 2*time.Second\\n                    cfg.LeaderLeaseTimeout = 2*time.Second\\n                }\\n                store := NewInmemStore()\\n                r,err := NewRaft(cfg,n.fsm,store,store,NewInmemSnapshotStore(),n.tr)\\n                if err!=nil { t.Fatal(err) }\\n                n.r=r\\n            }\\n            old := nodes[0]\\n            if err:=assuranceAwait(t,old.r.BootstrapCluster(Configuration{Servers:[]Server{{ID:old.id,Address:old.addr,Suffrage:Voter}}}),time.Second); err!=nil { t.Fatal(err) }\\n            assuranceUntil(t,6*time.Second,\\\"initial real single-voter election\\\",func()bool{return old.r.State()==Leader})\\n            for _,n:=range nodes[1:3] {\\n                if err:=assuranceAwait(t,old.r.AddVoter(n.id,n.addr,0,time.Second),2*time.Second); err!=nil { t.Fatal(err) }\\n            }\\n            nv:=nodes[3]\\n            cf:=old.r.AddNonvoter(nv.id,nv.addr,0,time.Second)\\n            if err:=assuranceAwait(t,cf,2*time.Second); err!=nil { t.Fatal(err) }\\n            configIndex:=cf.Index()\\n            before:=old.r.Apply([]byte(\\\"before\\\"),time.Second)\\n            if err:=assuranceAwait(t,before,2*time.Second); err!=nil { t.Fatal(err) }\\n            assuranceUntil(t,2*time.Second,\\\"all peers consume initial committed command\\\",func()bool{\\n                for _,n:=range nodes { if assuranceLast(n)!=\\\"before\\\" || n.r.CommitIndex()<configIndex {return false} }\\n                return true\\n            })\\n            for _,n:=range nodes {\\n                f:=n.r.GetConfiguration()\\n                if err:=assuranceAwait(t,f,time.Second); err!=nil {t.Fatal(err)}\\n                cfg:=f.Configuration()\\n                if len(cfg.Servers)!=4 {t.Fatalf(\\\"configuration prefix mismatch node=%s servers=%+v\\\",n.id,cfg.Servers)}\\n                voters:=0\\n                for _,s:=range cfg.Servers {\\n                    if s.Suffrage==Voter {voters++}\\n                    if s.ID==nv.id && s.Suffrage!=Nonvoter {t.Fatal(\\\"nonvoter prefix mismatch\\\")}\\n                }\\n                if voters!=3 {t.Fatal(\\\"voter count mismatch\\\")}\\n            }\\n            oldTerm:=old.r.CurrentTerm()\\n            assuranceEmit(\\\"prefix\\\",map[string]interface{}{\\\"run\\\":name,\\\"old_id\\\":string(old.id),\\\"old_term\\\":oldTerm,\\\"configuration_index\\\":configIndex,\\\"voters\\\":3,\\\"nonvoters\\\":1,\\\"initial_apply_index\\\":before.Index(),\\\"old_value\\\":assuranceLast(old)})\\n            healthyErr:=assuranceAwait(t,old.r.VerifyLeader(),time.Second)\\n            assuranceEmit(\\\"healthy_control\\\",map[string]interface{}{\\\"run\\\":name,\\\"ok\\\":healthyErr==nil,\\\"error\\\":fmt.Sprint(healthyErr)})\\n            if healthyErr!=nil {t.Fatal(healthyErr)}\\n\\n            // Separate {old, nonvoter} from the other two voters in both\\n            // directions. In the control, also separate old from nonvoter.\\n            cutStart:=time.Now()\\n            for _,i:=range []int{0,3} {\\n                for _,j:=range []int{1,2} {\\n                    nodes[i].tr.Disconnect(nodes[j].addr)\\n                    nodes[j].tr.Disconnect(nodes[i].addr)\\n                }\\n            }\\n            if !keepNonvoter {\\n                old.tr.Disconnect(nv.addr)\\n                nv.tr.Disconnect(old.addr)\\n            }\\n            assuranceEmit(\\\"partition\\\",map[string]interface{}{\\\"run\\\":name,\\\"nonvoter_connected\\\":keepNonvoter})\\n            var successor *assuranceNode\\n            assuranceUntil(t,1500*time.Millisecond,\\\"actual replacement voter election\\\",func()bool{\\n                for _,n:=range nodes[1:3] {\\n                    if n.r.State()==Leader && n.r.CurrentTerm()>oldTerm {successor=n;return true}\\n                }\\n                return false\\n            })\\n            after:=successor.r.Apply([]byte(\\\"after\\\"),time.Second)\\n            if err:=assuranceAwait(t,after,time.Second); err!=nil {t.Fatal(err)}\\n            newTerm:=successor.r.CurrentTerm()\\n            if successor.r.State()!=Leader || newTerm<=oldTerm || assuranceLast(successor)!=\\\"after\\\" {t.Fatal(\\\"replacement authority prerequisite changed\\\")}\\n            op:=name+\\\"_verify_after_new_write\\\"\\n            assuranceEmit(\\\"replacement_write\\\",map[string]interface{}{\\\"run\\\":name,\\\"op\\\":op,\\\"old_id\\\":string(old.id),\\\"new_id\\\":string(successor.id),\\\"old_term\\\":oldTerm,\\\"new_term\\\":newTerm,\\\"term_advanced\\\":newTerm>oldTerm,\\\"write_ok\\\":true,\\\"new_value\\\":assuranceLast(successor),\\\"write_index\\\":after.Index()})\\n            preCounts:=old.tr.counts()\\n            assuranceEmit(\\\"verify_invocation\\\",map[string]interface{}{\\\"run\\\":name,\\\"op\\\":op,\\\"old_id\\\":string(old.id),\\\"old_term\\\":old.r.CurrentTerm(),\\\"old_state\\\":old.r.State().String(),\\\"new_term\\\":newTerm,\\\"new_id\\\":string(successor.id),\\\"old_value\\\":assuranceLast(old),\\\"partition_elapsed_ms\\\":time.Since(cutStart).Milliseconds()})\\n            err:=assuranceAwait(t,old.r.VerifyLeader(),4*time.Second)\\n            // Record public result without asserting the disputed requirement.\\n            // The controller compares it with the fixed property independently.\\n            assuranceEmit(\\\"verify_result\\\",map[string]interface{}{\\\"run\\\":name,\\\"op\\\":op,\\\"ok\\\":err==nil,\\\"error\\\":fmt.Sprint(err),\\\"old_id\\\":string(old.id),\\\"old_term\\\":old.r.CurrentTerm(),\\\"old_state\\\":old.r.State().String(),\\\"new_id\\\":string(successor.id),\\\"new_term\\\":successor.r.CurrentTerm(),\\\"new_state\\\":successor.r.State().String(),\\\"old_value\\\":assuranceLast(old),\\\"new_value\\\":assuranceLast(successor),\\\"before_replies\\\":preCounts,\\\"after_replies\\\":old.tr.counts(),\\\"partition_elapsed_ms\\\":time.Since(cutStart).Milliseconds()})\\n        })\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\n    \"description\": \"TestAssuranceVerifyAuthorityHistory: independent with_nonvoter and without_nonvoter_contact subtests, real bootstrap/elections/membership/application, controlled route cuts, then public VerifyLeader.Error.\",\n    \"semantic_changes\": [\n      \"A transport wrapper counts successful real AppendEntries returns without modifying requests or responses.\",\n      \"The wrapper declines the optional pipeline with ErrPipelineReplicationNotSupported; ordinary replication is retained.\",\n      \"MockFSM is the repository implementation and is read under its mutex; no FSM mutation is injected.\",\n      \"Nonuniform but individually validated node-local timeouts create a finite observation window while every lease/election worker remains active.\",\n      \"No target source or dependency definitions are changed.\"\n    ],\n    \"prerequisites\": [\n      {\n        \"alias\": \"replacement\",\n        \"event\": \"replacement_write\",\n        \"conditions\": [\n          {\n            \"field\": \"term_advanced\",\n            \"op\": \"eq\",\n            \"value\": true,\n            \"reference\": null\n          },\n          {\n            \"field\": \"write_ok\",\n            \"op\": \"eq\",\n            \"value\": true,\n            \"reference\": null\n          },\n          {\n            \"field\": \"new_id\",\n            \"op\": \"ne\",\n            \"value\": \"\",\n            \"reference\": null\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"alias\": \"invoked\",\n        \"event\": \"verify_invocation\",\n        \"conditions\": [\n          {\n            \"field\": \"new_id\",\n            \"op\": \"eq\",\n            \"value\": null,\n            \"reference\": \"replacement.new_id\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"legality\": {\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"S-bootstrap\",\n        \"S-startup\",\n        \"S-membership-api\",\n        \"S-config-dispatch\",\n        \"S-repl-membership\",\n        \"S-election\",\n        \"S-vote-producer\",\n        \"S-control-config\",\n        \"S-control-config-validation\",\n        \"S-control-transport\",\n        \"S-replicate\",\n        \"S-api-apply\",\n        \"S-fsm-worker\",\n        \"S-mock-fsm\",\n        \"S-observation-api\",\n        \"S-config-observation\",\n        \"S-lease\",\n        \"S-leader-session\"\n      ],\n      \"expectation_ids\": [\n        \"S-control-config\",\n        \"S-future-completion\",\n        \"S-api-apply\"\n      ],\n      \"binding_ids\": [\n        \"L-verify-api\",\n        \"L-verify-registration\",\n        \"L-verify-count\",\n        \"L-verify-completion\"\n      ],\n      \"derivation\": \"O-verify-current-authority is tested through L-verify-api/L-verify-completion. Four real Raft instances start with empty in-memory stores and default background workers. BootstrapCluster on the designated old peer creates a single-voter prefix and its actual timer-driven election. Successful sequential AddVoter, AddVoter and AddNonvoter calls create the final stable configuration. A real Apply completes; the harness waits for all FSMs to contain its value and all CommitIndex values to cross the configuration entry. Latest membership contents are checked using GetConfiguration; the configuration entry index is taken from the successful membership future, because GetConfiguration constructs no latestIndex. InmemTransport Disconnect cuts every cross-component direction. The replacement is observed through State/CurrentTerm and its actual successful Apply future before old VerifyLeader is invoked.\",\n      \"applicability\": \"One component contains the former leader and optionally its nonvoter link; the other contains the two other voters. Ordinary AppendEntries, heartbeats, elections, lease checks, FSM and snapshot workers all run. Newer-term negative replies from the majority are prevented by the network cut, not bypassed in protocol code. Old local lease is 2s, with 2s heartbeat/election timeouts; others use 100ms heartbeat, 150ms election and 80ms lease. CommitTimeout=5ms supplies frequent ordinary contact before the cut. Each Config is actually validated by NewRaft. Optional pipelining is declined via its supported ErrPipelineReplicationNotSupported fallback so all traffic follows the controlled in-memory routes. Counters only observe successful real RPC returns. In-memory storage represents a crash-free execution; it does not provide production durability evidence. The two subtests are independent complete histories, never concatenated into one.\",\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"The result isolates a public contract discrepancy; exact vote-edge causality is supported by source and reply counters, not by instrumentation inside notifyAll.\",\n        \"Different configured node timeouts are intentional and scoped. No conclusion is made about a uniform-timeout deployment.\"\n      ],\n      \"conflicts\": [],\n      \"alternatives\": [\n        \"The no-nonvoter-contact control leaves lease cleanup running and waits for actual verification completion rather than treating silence as failure.\",\n        \"Healthy connected verification must complete successfully before partition; failure aborts that history as an unreached prerequisite.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  \"monitors\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"M-verify-after-replacement\",\n      \"checker_id\": \"P-no-obsolete-verification\",\n      \"event\": \"verify_result\",\n      \"binding_ids\": [\n        \"L-verify-api\",\n        \"L-verify-registration\",\n        \"L-verify-count\",\n        \"L-verify-completion\"\n      ],\n      \"grounding\": {\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"S-api-verify\",\n          \"S-verify-register\",\n          \"S-verify-vote\",\n          \"S-leader-loop\",\n          \"S-future-error\",\n          \"S-future-completion\",\n          \"S-election\",\n          \"S-api-apply\",\n          \"S-fsm-worker\",\n          \"S-observation-api\"\n        ],\n        \"expectation_ids\": [\n          \"S-api-verify\"\n        ],\n        \"binding_ids\": [\n          \"L-verify-api\",\n          \"L-verify-registration\",\n          \"L-verify-count\",\n          \"L-verify-completion\"\n        ],\n        \"derivation\": \"For O-verify-current-authority and L-verify-api/L-verify-completion, replacement_write records a successful actual Apply on a distinct elected peer at a term numerically greater than the old term. verify_invocation follows that event and selects the same replacement participant through an explicit predecessor reference. A generated op identifies the one invocation independently of term and success. verify_result records the actual Future.Error return as ok=(err==nil), plus raw term/state/FSM values. The oracle requires ok=false for this admitted obsolete-authority invocation. It does not require success merely because support might be sufficient, and does not infer general liveness from waiting.\",\n        \"applicability\": \"Admission is verify_invocation after its correlated replacement_write, not the first prerequisite by order. Both histories keep the old peer cut off from the voting majority. Identity is op only; mutable terms, roles and results are not identity filters. The driver ends by waiting for the real future or declaring an incomplete deadline, then shuts all nodes down. Any failure in a prefix stops that history before admission. Healthy-control events are separate setup diagnostics, not prerequisites or results for this monitor.\",\n        \"unresolved\": [\n          \"Raw old/new FSM values demonstrate the application states sampled around this API invocation; no separate externally served read API is executed.\",\n          \"Transport counts do not rule out every already-returned pre-partition reply being scheduled late, so they alone do not prove the exact cause.\"\n        ],\n        \"conflicts\": [],\n        \"alternatives\": []\n      },\n      \"applicability_conditions\": [],\n      \"admission_alias\": \"invoked\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"observable_properties\": [\n    {\n      \"checker_id\": \"P-no-obsolete-verification\",\n      \"kind\": \"event_assertion\",\n      \"trigger\": {\n        \"field\": \"event\",\n        \"op\": \"eq\",\n        \"value\": \"verify_result\",\n        \"reference\": null\n      },\n      \"assertion\": {\n        \"field\": \"ok\",\n        \"op\": \"eq\",\n        \"value\": false,\n        \"reference\": null\n      },\n      \"antecedent\": null,\n      \"identity_fields\": [\n        \"op\"\n      ],\n      \"history_field\": null,\n      \"description\": \"After a real replacement leader completes its command before invocation, the isolated old peer must not return successful VerifyLeader assurance.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"uncertainties\": [\n    \"Only protocol v3, fixed three-voter/one-nonvoter membership, crash-free in-memory storage and nonpipelined transport are exercised.\",\n    \"All timeouts bound construction/observation only. An unreached prefix or missing return is unknown, not holds or a liveness finding.\",\n    \"Public verification failure in the no-contact control need not occur at an exact deadline or with an exact error string.\",\n    \"The two executions compare connectivity; their election terms, participants and replies are correlated only within each subtest.\",\n    \"This check does not claim invalid log commitment or a production application read violation.\"\n  ]\n}\nFIXED HARNESS package raft\n\nimport (\n    \"encoding/json\"\n    \"fmt\"\n    \"io\"\n    \"sync\"\n    \"testing\"\n    \"time\"\n)\n\n// The transport retains the real in-memory RPC producer/receiver paths. The\n// optional pipeline is disabled so a partition cuts the same routes for every\n// AppendEntries call; successful responses are never synthesized.\ntype assuranceTransport struct {\n    *InmemTransport\n    mu sync.Mutex\n    replies map[ServerID]int\n}\n\nfunc (a *assuranceTransport) AppendEntriesPipeline(id ServerID, addr ServerAddress) (AppendPipeline, error) {\n    return nil, ErrPipelineReplicationNotSupported\n}\n\nfunc (a *assuranceTransport) AppendEntries(id ServerID, addr ServerAddress, req *AppendEntriesRequest, resp *AppendEntriesResponse) error {\n    err := a.InmemTransport.AppendEntries(id, addr, req, resp)\n    if err == nil && resp.Success {\n        a.mu.Lock()\n        a.replies[id]++\n        a.mu.Unlock()\n    }\n    return err\n}\n\nfunc (a *assuranceTransport) counts() map[string]int {\n    a.mu.Lock()\n    defer a.mu.Unlock()\n    c := make(map[string]int)\n    for k, v := range a.replies { c[string(k)] = v }\n    return c\n}\n\ntype assuranceNode struct {\n    r *Raft\n    tr *assuranceTransport\n    fsm *MockFSM\n    id ServerID\n    addr ServerAddress\n}\n\nfunc assuranceEmit(event string, fields map[string]interface{}) {\n    fields[\"event\"] = event\n    b, err := json.Marshal(fields)\n    if err != nil { panic(err) }\n    fmt.Println(\"CA_EVENT \" + string(b))\n}\n\nfunc assuranceAwait(t *testing.T, f Future, d time.Duration) error {\n    t.Helper()\n    ch := make(chan error, 1)\n    go func() { ch <- f.Error() }()\n    select {\n    case err := <-ch: return err\n    case <-time.After(d): t.Fatal(\"future completion deadline: observation is incomplete\"); return nil\n    }\n}\n\nfunc assuranceUntil(t *testing.T, d time.Duration, what string, pred func() bool) {\n    t.Helper()\n    stop := time.Now().Add(d)\n    for time.Now().Before(stop) {\n        if pred() { return }\n        time.Sleep(2*time.Millisecond)\n    }\n    t.Fatalf(\"unreached prerequisite: %s\", what)\n}\n\nfunc assuranceLast(n *assuranceNode) string {\n    n.fsm.Lock()\n    defer n.fsm.Unlock()\n    if len(n.fsm.logs)==0 { return \"\" }\n    return string(n.fsm.logs[len(n.fsm.logs)-1])\n}\n\nfunc TestAssuranceVerifyAuthorityHistory(t *testing.T) {\n    for _, keepNonvoter := range []bool{true, false} {\n        name := \"with_nonvoter\"\n        if !keepNonvoter { name = \"without_nonvoter_contact\" }\n        t.Run(name, func(t *testing.T) {\n            nodes := make([]*assuranceNode, 4)\n            for i := range nodes {\n                id := ServerID(fmt.Sprintf(\"%s_node_%d\", name, i))\n                addr, base := NewInmemTransportWithTimeout(ServerAddress(id), 40*time.Millisecond)\n                nodes[i] = &assuranceNode{id:id, addr:addr, tr:&assuranceTransport{InmemTransport:base, replies:make(map[ServerID]int)}, fsm:&MockFSM{}}\n            }\n            for i,n := range nodes {\n                for j,p := range nodes {\n                    if i!=j { n.tr.Connect(p.addr, p.tr.InmemTransport) }\n                }\n            }\n            defer func() {\n                // Initiate shutdown for all nodes before waiting for any one.\n                var fs []Future\n                for _,n := range nodes { if n.r!=nil { fs=append(fs,n.r.Shutdown()) } }\n                for _,n := range nodes { n.tr.Close() }\n                for _,f := range fs { assuranceAwait(t,f,3*time.Second) }\n            }()\n            for i,n := range nodes {\n                cfg := DefaultConfig()\n                cfg.ProtocolVersion = 3\n                cfg.LocalID = n.id\n                cfg.LogOutput = io.Discard\n                cfg.CommitTimeout = 5*time.Millisecond\n                cfg.HeartbeatTimeout = 100*time.Millisecond\n                cfg.ElectionTimeout = 150*time.Millisecond\n                cfg.LeaderLeaseTimeout = 80*time.Millisecond\n                if i==0 {\n                    // A longer local lease leaves an observable interval after\n                    // the remote voters elect. All safety/lease workers still run.\n                    cfg.HeartbeatTimeout = 2*time.Second\n                    cfg.ElectionTimeout = 2*time.Second\n                    cfg.LeaderLeaseTimeout = 2*time.Second\n                }\n                store := NewInmemStore()\n                r,err := NewRaft(cfg,n.fsm,store,store,NewInmemSnapshotStore(),n.tr)\n                if err!=nil { t.Fatal(err) }\n                n.r=r\n            }\n            old := nodes[0]\n            if err:=assuranceAwait(t,old.r.BootstrapCluster(Configuration{Servers:[]Server{{ID:old.id,Address:old.addr,Suffrage:Voter}}}),time.Second); err!=nil { t.Fatal(err) }\n            assuranceUntil(t,6*time.Second,\"initial real single-voter election\",func()bool{return old.r.State()==Leader})\n            for _,n:=range nodes[1:3] {\n                if err:=assuranceAwait(t,old.r.AddVoter(n.id,n.addr,0,time.Second),2*time.Second); err!=nil { t.Fatal(err) }\n            }\n            nv:=nodes[3]\n            cf:=old.r.AddNonvoter(nv.id,nv.addr,0,time.Second)\n            if err:=assuranceAwait(t,cf,2*time.Second); err!=nil { t.Fatal(err) }\n            configIndex:=cf.Index()\n            before:=old.r.Apply([]byte(\"before\"),time.Second)\n            if err:=assuranceAwait(t,before,2*time.Second); err!=nil { t.Fatal(err) }\n            assuranceUntil(t,2*time.Second,\"all peers consume initial committed command\",func()bool{\n                for _,n:=range nodes { if assuranceLast(n)!=\"before\" || n.r.CommitIndex()<configIndex {return false} }\n                return true\n            })\n            for _,n:=range nodes {\n                f:=n.r.GetConfiguration()\n                if err:=assuranceAwait(t,f,time.Second); err!=nil {t.Fatal(err)}\n                cfg:=f.Configuration()\n                if len(cfg.Servers)!=4 {t.Fatalf(\"configuration prefix mismatch node=%s servers=%+v\",n.id,cfg.Servers)}\n                voters:=0\n                for _,s:=range cfg.Servers {\n                    if s.Suffrage==Voter {voters++}\n                    if s.ID==nv.id && s.Suffrage!=Nonvoter {t.Fatal(\"nonvoter prefix mismatch\")}\n                }\n                if voters!=3 {t.Fatal(\"voter count mismatch\")}\n            }\n            oldTerm:=old.r.CurrentTerm()\n            assuranceEmit(\"prefix\",map[string]interface{}{\"run\":name,\"old_id\":string(old.id),\"old_term\":oldTerm,\"configuration_index\":configIndex,\"voters\":3,\"nonvoters\":1,\"initial_apply_index\":before.Index(),\"old_value\":assuranceLast(old)})\n            healthyErr:=assuranceAwait(t,old.r.VerifyLeader(),time.Second)\n            assuranceEmit(\"healthy_control\",map[string]interface{}{\"run\":name,\"ok\":healthyErr==nil,\"error\":fmt.Sprint(healthyErr)})\n            if healthyErr!=nil {t.Fatal(healthyErr)}\n\n            // Separate {old, nonvoter} from the other two voters in both\n            // directions. In the control, also separate old from nonvoter.\n            cutStart:=time.Now()\n            for _,i:=range []int{0,3} {\n                for _,j:=range []int{1,2} {\n                    nodes[i].tr.Disconnect(nodes[j].addr)\n                    nodes[j].tr.Disconnect(nodes[i].addr)\n                }\n            }\n            if !keepNonvoter {\n                old.tr.Disconnect(nv.addr)\n                nv.tr.Disconnect(old.addr)\n            }\n            assuranceEmit(\"partition\",map[string]interface{}{\"run\":name,\"nonvoter_connected\":keepNonvoter})\n            var successor *assuranceNode\n            assuranceUntil(t,1500*time.Millisecond,\"actual replacement voter election\",func()bool{\n                for _,n:=range nodes[1:3] {\n                    if n.r.State()==Leader && n.r.CurrentTerm()>oldTerm {successor=n;return true}\n                }\n                return false\n            })\n            after:=successor.r.Apply([]byte(\"after\"),time.Second)\n            if err:=assuranceAwait(t,after,time.Second); err!=nil {t.Fatal(err)}\n            newTerm:=successor.r.CurrentTerm()\n            if successor.r.State()!=Leader || newTerm<=oldTerm || assuranceLast(successor)!=\"after\" {t.Fatal(\"replacement authority prerequisite changed\")}\n            op:=name+\"_verify_after_new_write\"\n            assuranceEmit(\"replacement_write\",map[string]interface{}{\"run\":name,\"op\":op,\"old_id\":string(old.id),\"new_id\":string(successor.id),\"old_term\":oldTerm,\"new_term\":newTerm,\"term_advanced\":newTerm>oldTerm,\"write_ok\":true,\"new_value\":assuranceLast(successor),\"write_index\":after.Index()})\n            preCounts:=old.tr.counts()\n            assuranceEmit(\"verify_invocation\",map[string]interface{}{\"run\":name,\"op\":op,\"old_id\":string(old.id),\"old_term\":old.r.CurrentTerm(),\"old_state\":old.r.State().String(),\"new_term\":newTerm,\"new_id\":string(successor.id),\"old_value\":assuranceLast(old),\"partition_elapsed_ms\":time.Since(cutStart).Milliseconds()})\n            err:=assuranceAwait(t,old.r.VerifyLeader(),4*time.Second)\n            // Record public result without asserting the disputed requirement.\n            // The controller compares it with the fixed property independently.\n            assuranceEmit(\"verify_result\",map[string]interface{}{\"run\":name,\"op\":op,\"ok\":err==nil,\"error\":fmt.Sprint(err),\"old_id\":string(old.id),\"old_term\":old.r.CurrentTerm(),\"old_state\":old.r.State().String(),\"new_id\":string(successor.id),\"new_term\":successor.r.CurrentTerm(),\"new_state\":successor.r.State().String(),\"old_value\":assuranceLast(old),\"new_value\":assuranceLast(successor),\"before_replies\":preCounts,\"after_replies\":old.tr.counts(),\"partition_elapsed_ms\":time.Since(cutStart).Milliseconds()})\n        })\n    }\n}\n\nREVIEW_SCHEMA {\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"target_id\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"default\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Target Id\"\n    },\n    \"aspect\": {\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"applicability\",\n        \"decomposition\",\n        \"checker_correspondence\"\n      ],\n      \"title\": \"Aspect\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"status\": {\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"no_issue_found\",\n        \"needs_reading\",\n        \"disputed\",\n        \"revision_needed\"\n      ],\n      \"title\": \"Status\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"source_ids\": {\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"title\": \"Source Ids\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"rationale\": {\n      \"title\": \"Rationale\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"counterevidence\": {\n      \"default\": [],\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Counterevidence\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"limitations\": {\n      \"default\": [],\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Limitations\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"challenged_components\": {\n      \"description\": \"Components requiring repair, distinct from the review aspect; revision_needed must name them\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"enum\": [\n          \"configuration\",\n          \"initialization\",\n          \"driver\",\n          \"observation\",\n          \"oracle\",\n          \"expectation\",\n          \"scope\"\n        ],\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Challenged Components\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"aspect\",\n    \"status\",\n    \"source_ids\",\n    \"rationale\"\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"ArtifactReviewItem\",\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat ../logs/bcaed4ce26bf44d797a18ec78b37a154/stdout.log; cat ../logs/bcaed4ce26bf44d797a18ec78b37a154/stderr.log; grep -R -n -i --include='*.go' --include='*.md' -E 'same.*timeout|timeout.*same|VerifyLeader|lineariz|stale read' ../agent-source | head -65; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np=json.load(open('../direct-checks/f0fd7479adcd418884ccfb446842e310/plan.json'));p['harness'].pop('source')\nprint(json.dumps(p,indent=2))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat ../logs/bcaed4ce26bf44d797a18ec78b37a154/stdout.log; cat ../logs/bcaed4ce26bf44d797a18ec78b37a154/stderr.log; grep -R -n -i --include='*.go' --include='*.md' -E 'same.*timeout|timeout.*same|VerifyLeader|lineariz|stale read' ../agent-source | head -65; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np=json.load(open('../direct-checks/f0fd7479adcd418884ccfb446842e310/plan.json'));p['harness'].pop('source')\nprint(json.dumps(p,indent=2))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"description\": \"Replace the accepted candidate's prefix, producer and public-endpoint gaps using real four-node histories. Compare old VerifyLeader after a newer leader completes a command with and without connectivity to the nonvoter. Observe completed futures and raw FSM values; the controller applies an independent no-success-after-supersession oracle.\",\n  \"claim_id\": \"O-verify-current-authority\",\n  \"binding_ids\": [\n    \"L-verify-api\",\n    \"L-verify-registration\",\n    \"L-verify-count\",\n    \"L-verify-completion\"\n  ],\n  \"harness\": {\n    \"files\": {},\n    \"kind\": \"go_test\",\n    \"description\": \"TestAssuranceVerifyAuthorityHistory: independent with_nonvoter and without_nonvoter_contact subtests, real bootstrap/elections/membership/application, controlled route cuts, then public VerifyLeader.Error.\",\n    \"semantic_changes\": [\n      \"A transport wrapper counts successful real AppendEntries returns without modifying requests or responses.\",\n      \"The wrapper declines the optional pipeline with ErrPipelineReplicationNotSupported; ordinary replication is retained.\",\n      \"MockFSM is the repository implementation and is read under its mutex; no FSM mutation is injected.\",\n      \"Nonuniform but individually validated node-local timeouts create a finite observation window while every lease/election worker remains active.\",\n      \"No target source or dependency definitions are changed.\"\n    ],\n    \"prerequisites\": [\n      {\n        \"alias\": \"replacement\",\n        \"event\": \"replacement_write\",\n        \"conditions\": [\n          {\n            \"field\": \"term_advanced\",\n            \"op\": \"eq\",\n            \"value\": true,\n            \"reference\": null\n          },\n          {\n            \"field\": \"write_ok\",\n            \"op\": \"eq\",\n            \"value\": true,\n            \"reference\": null\n          },\n          {\n            \"field\": \"new_id\",\n            \"op\": \"ne\",\n            \"value\": \"\",\n            \"reference\": null\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"alias\": \"invoked\",\n        \"event\": \"verify_invocation\",\n        \"conditions\": [\n          {\n            \"field\": \"new_id\",\n            \"op\": \"eq\",\n            \"value\": null,\n            \"reference\": \"replacement.new_id\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"legality\": {\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"S-bootstrap\",\n        \"S-startup\",\n        \"S-membership-api\",\n        \"S-config-dispatch\",\n        \"S-repl-membership\",\n        \"S-election\",\n        \"S-vote-producer\",\n        \"S-control-config\",\n        \"S-control-config-validation\",\n        \"S-control-transport\",\n        \"S-replicate\",\n        \"S-api-apply\",\n        \"S-fsm-worker\",\n        \"S-mock-fsm\",\n        \"S-observation-api\",\n        \"S-config-observation\",\n        \"S-lease\",\n        \"S-leader-session\"\n      ],\n      \"expectation_ids\": [\n        \"S-control-config\",\n        \"S-future-completion\",\n        \"S-api-apply\"\n      ],\n      \"binding_ids\": [\n        \"L-verify-api\",\n        \"L-verify-registration\",\n        \"L-verify-count\",\n        \"L-verify-completion\"\n      ],\n      \"derivation\": \"O-verify-current-authority is tested through L-verify-api/L-verify-completion. Four real Raft instances start with empty in-memory stores and default background workers. BootstrapCluster on the designated old peer creates a single-voter prefix and its actual timer-driven election. Successful sequential AddVoter, AddVoter and AddNonvoter calls create the final stable configuration. A real Apply completes; the harness waits for all FSMs to contain its value and all CommitIndex values to cross the configuration entry. Latest membership contents are checked using GetConfiguration; the configuration entry index is taken from the successful membership future, because GetConfiguration constructs no latestIndex. InmemTransport Disconnect cuts every cross-component direction. The replacement is observed through State/CurrentTerm and its actual successful Apply future before old VerifyLeader is invoked.\",\n      \"applicability\": \"One component contains the former leader and optionally its nonvoter link; the other contains the two other voters. Ordinary AppendEntries, heartbeats, elections, lease checks, FSM and snapshot workers all run. Newer-term negative replies from the majority are prevented by the network cut, not bypassed in protocol code. Old local lease is 2s, with 2s heartbeat/election timeouts; others use 100ms heartbeat, 150ms election and 80ms lease. CommitTimeout=5ms supplies frequent ordinary contact before the cut. Each Config is actually validated by NewRaft. Optional pipelining is declined via its supported ErrPipelineReplicationNotSupported fallback so all traffic follows the controlled in-memory routes. Counters only observe successful real RPC returns. In-memory storage represents a crash-free execution; it does not provide production durability evidence. The two subtests are independent complete histories, never concatenated into one.\",\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"The result isolates a public contract discrepancy; exact vote-edge causality is supported by source and reply counters, not by instrumentation inside notifyAll.\",\n        \"Different configured node timeouts are intentional and scoped. No conclusion is made about a uniform-timeout deployment.\"\n      ],\n      \"conflicts\": [],\n      \"alternatives\": [\n        \"The no-nonvoter-contact control leaves lease cleanup running and waits for actual verification completion rather than treating silence as failure.\",\n        \"Healthy connected verification must complete successfully before partition; failure aborts that history as an unreached prerequisite.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  \"monitors\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"M-verify-after-replacement\",\n      \"checker_id\": \"P-no-obsolete-verification\",\n      \"event\": \"verify_result\",\n      \"binding_ids\": [\n        \"L-verify-api\",\n        \"L-verify-registration\",\n        \"L-verify-count\",\n        \"L-verify-completion\"\n      ],\n      \"grounding\": {\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"S-api-verify\",\n          \"S-verify-register\",\n          \"S-verify-vote\",\n          \"S-leader-loop\",\n          \"S-future-error\",\n          \"S-future-completion\",\n          \"S-election\",\n          \"S-api-apply\",\n          \"S-fsm-worker\",\n          \"S-observation-api\"\n        ],\n        \"expectation_ids\": [\n          \"S-api-verify\"\n        ],\n        \"binding_ids\": [\n          \"L-verify-api\",\n          \"L-verify-registration\",\n          \"L-verify-count\",\n          \"L-verify-completion\"\n        ],\n        \"derivation\": \"For O-verify-current-authority and L-verify-api/L-verify-completion, replacement_write records a successful actual Apply on a distinct elected peer at a term numerically greater than the old term. verify_invocation follows that event and selects the same replacement participant through an explicit predecessor reference. A generated op identifies the one invocation independently of term and success. verify_result records the actual Future.Error return as ok=(err==nil), plus raw term/state/FSM values. The oracle requires ok=false for this admitted obsolete-authority invocation. It does not require success merely because support might be sufficient, and does not infer general liveness from waiting.\",\n        \"applicability\": \"Admission is verify_invocation after its correlated replacement_write, not the first prerequisite by order. Both histories keep the old peer cut off from the voting majority. Identity is op only; mutable terms, roles and results are not identity filters. The driver ends by waiting for the real future or declaring an incomplete deadline, then shuts all nodes down. Any failure in a prefix stops that history before admission. Healthy-control events are separate setup diagnostics, not prerequisites or results for this monitor.\",\n        \"unresolved\": [\n          \"Raw old/new FSM values demonstrate the application states sampled around this API invocation; no separate externally served read API is executed.\",\n          \"Transport counts do not rule out every already-returned pre-partition reply being scheduled late, so they alone do not prove the exact cause.\"\n        ],\n        \"conflicts\": [],\n        \"alternatives\": []\n      },\n      \"applicability_conditions\": [],\n      \"admission_alias\": \"invoked\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"observable_properties\": [\n    {\n      \"checker_id\": \"P-no-obsolete-verification\",\n      \"kind\": \"event_assertion\",\n      \"trigger\": {\n        \"field\": \"event\",\n        \"op\": \"eq\",\n        \"value\": \"verify_result\",\n        \"reference\": null\n      },\n      \"assertion\": {\n        \"field\": \"ok\",\n        \"op\": \"eq\",\n        \"value\": false,\n        \"reference\": null\n      },\n      \"antecedent\": null,\n      \"identity_fields\": [\n        \"op\"\n      ],\n      \"history_field\": null,\n      \"description\": \"After a real replacement leader completes its command before invocation, the isolated old peer must not return successful VerifyLeader assurance.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"uncertainties\": [\n    \"Only protocol v3, fixed three-voter/one-nonvoter membership, crash-free in-memory storage and nonpipelined transport are exercised.\",\n    \"All timeouts bound construction/observation only. An unreached prefix or missing return is unknown, not holds or a liveness finding.\",\n    \"Public verification failure in the no-contact control need not occur at an exact deadline or with an exact error string.\",\n    \"The two executions compare connectivity; their election terms, participants and replies are correlated only within each subtest.\",\n    \"This check does not claim invalid log commitment or a production application read violation.\"\n  ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba ../agent-source/docs/README.md | sed -n '34,103p'; nl -ba ../agent-source/README.md | sed -n '58,82p'; nl -ba ../agent-source/future.go | sed -n '226,250p'; nl -ba ../agent-source/config.go | sed -n '333,377p'; nl -ba ../agent-source/replication.go | sed -n '100,113p'; nl -ba ../agent-source/raft.go | sed -n '1033,1093p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba ../agent-source/docs/README.md | sed -n '34,103p'; nl -ba ../agent-source/README.md | sed -n '58,82p'; nl -ba ../agent-source/future.go | sed -n '226,250p'; nl -ba ../agent-source/config.go | sed -n '333,377p'; nl -ba ../agent-source/replication.go | sed -n '100,113p'; nl -ba ../agent-source/raft.go | sed -n '1033,1093p'\"","aggregated_output":"    58\t\n    59\t## Protocol\n    60\t\n    61\traft is based on [\"Raft: In Search of an Understandable Consensus Algorithm\"](https://raft.github.io/raft.pdf)\n    62\t\n    63\tA high level overview of the Raft protocol is described below, but for details please read the full\n    64\t[Raft paper](https://raft.github.io/raft.pdf)\n    65\tfollowed by the raft source. Any questions about the raft protocol should be sent to the\n    66\t[raft-dev mailing list](https://groups.google.com/forum/#!forum/raft-dev).\n    67\t\n    68\t### Protocol Description\n    69\t\n    70\tRaft nodes are always in one of three states: follower, candidate or leader. All\n    71\tnodes initially start out as a follower. In this state, nodes can accept log entries\n    72\tfrom a leader and cast votes. If no entries are received for some time, nodes\n    73\tself-promote to the candidate state. In the candidate state nodes request votes from\n    74\ttheir peers. If a candidate receives a quorum of votes, then it is promoted to a leader.\n    75\tThe leader must accept new log entries and replicate to all the other followers.\n    76\tIn addition, if stale reads are not acceptable, all queries must also be performed on\n    77\tthe leader.\n    78\t\n    79\tOnce a cluster has a leader, it is able to accept new log entries. A client can\n    80\trequest that a leader append a new log entry, which is an opaque binary blob to\n    81\tRaft. The leader then writes the entry to durable storage and attempts to replicate\n    82\tto a quorum of followers. Once the log entry is considered *committed*, it can be\n   226\t\tsnapshot FSMSnapshot\n   227\t}\n   228\t\n   229\t// restoreFuture is used for requesting an FSM to perform a\n   230\t// snapshot restore. Used internally only.\n   231\ttype restoreFuture struct {\n   232\t\tdeferError\n   233\t\tID string\n   234\t}\n   235\t\n   236\t// verifyFuture is used to verify the current node is still\n   237\t// the leader. This is to prevent a stale read.\n   238\ttype verifyFuture struct {\n   239\t\tdeferError\n   240\t\tnotifyCh   chan *verifyFuture\n   241\t\tquorumSize int\n   242\t\tvotes      int\n   243\t\tvoteLock   sync.Mutex\n   244\t}\n   245\t\n   246\t// leadershipTransferFuture is used to track the progress of a leadership\n   247\t// transfer internally.\n   248\ttype leadershipTransferFuture struct {\n   249\t\tdeferError\n   250\t\n   333\tfunc ValidateConfig(config *Config) error {\n   334\t\t// We don't actually support running as 0 in the library any more, but\n   335\t\t// we do understand it.\n   336\t\tprotocolMin := ProtocolVersionMin\n   337\t\tif protocolMin == 0 {\n   338\t\t\tprotocolMin = 1\n   339\t\t}\n   340\t\tif config.ProtocolVersion < protocolMin ||\n   341\t\t\tconfig.ProtocolVersion > ProtocolVersionMax {\n   342\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"ProtocolVersion %d must be >= %d and <= %d\",\n   343\t\t\t\tconfig.ProtocolVersion, protocolMin, ProtocolVersionMax)\n   344\t\t}\n   345\t\tif len(config.LocalID) == 0 {\n   346\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"LocalID cannot be empty\")\n   347\t\t}\n   348\t\tif config.HeartbeatTimeout < 5*time.Millisecond {\n   349\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"HeartbeatTimeout is too low\")\n   350\t\t}\n   351\t\tif config.ElectionTimeout < 5*time.Millisecond {\n   352\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"ElectionTimeout is too low\")\n   353\t\t}\n   354\t\tif config.CommitTimeout < time.Millisecond {\n   355\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"CommitTimeout is too low\")\n   356\t\t}\n   357\t\tif config.MaxAppendEntries <= 0 {\n   358\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"MaxAppendEntries must be positive\")\n   359\t\t}\n   360\t\tif config.MaxAppendEntries > 1024 {\n   361\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"MaxAppendEntries is too large\")\n   362\t\t}\n   363\t\tif config.SnapshotInterval < 5*time.Millisecond {\n   364\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"SnapshotInterval is too low\")\n   365\t\t}\n   366\t\tif config.LeaderLeaseTimeout < 5*time.Millisecond {\n   367\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"LeaderLeaseTimeout is too low\")\n   368\t\t}\n   369\t\tif config.LeaderLeaseTimeout > config.HeartbeatTimeout {\n   370\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"LeaderLeaseTimeout (%s) cannot be larger than heartbeat timeout (%s)\", config.LeaderLeaseTimeout, config.HeartbeatTimeout)\n   371\t\t}\n   372\t\tif config.ElectionTimeout < config.HeartbeatTimeout {\n   373\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"ElectionTimeout (%s) must be equal or greater than Heartbeat Timeout (%s)\", config.ElectionTimeout, config.HeartbeatTimeout)\n   374\t\t}\n   375\t\treturn nil\n   376\t}\n   100\tfunc (s *followerReplication) notifyAll(leader bool) {\n   101\t\t// Clear the waiting notifies minimizing lock time\n   102\t\ts.notifyLock.Lock()\n   103\t\tn := s.notify\n   104\t\ts.notify = make(map[*verifyFuture]struct{})\n   105\t\ts.notifyLock.Unlock()\n   106\t\n   107\t\t// Submit our votes\n   108\t\tfor v := range n {\n   109\t\t\tv.vote(leader)\n   110\t\t}\n   111\t}\n   112\t\n   113\t// cleanNotify is used to delete notify, .\n  1033\t// within the last leader lease interval. If not, we need to step down,\n  1034\t// as we may have lost connectivity. Returns the maximum duration without\n  1035\t// contact. This must only be called from the main thread.\n  1036\tfunc (r *Raft) checkLeaderLease() time.Duration {\n  1037\t\t// Track contacted nodes, we can always contact ourself\n  1038\t\tcontacted := 0\n  1039\t\n  1040\t\t// Store lease timeout for this one check invocation as we need to refer to it\n  1041\t\t// in the loop and would be confusing if it ever becomes reloadable and\n  1042\t\t// changes between iterations below.\n  1043\t\tleaseTimeout := r.config().LeaderLeaseTimeout\n  1044\t\n  1045\t\t// Check each follower\n  1046\t\tvar maxDiff time.Duration\n  1047\t\tnow := time.Now()\n  1048\t\tfor _, server := range r.configurations.latest.Servers {\n  1049\t\t\tif server.Suffrage == Voter {\n  1050\t\t\t\tif server.ID == r.localID {\n  1051\t\t\t\t\tcontacted++\n  1052\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n  1053\t\t\t\t}\n  1054\t\t\t\tf := r.leaderState.replState[server.ID]\n  1055\t\t\t\tdiff := now.Sub(f.LastContact())\n  1056\t\t\t\tif diff <= leaseTimeout {\n  1057\t\t\t\t\tcontacted++\n  1058\t\t\t\t\tif diff > maxDiff {\n  1059\t\t\t\t\t\tmaxDiff = diff\n  1060\t\t\t\t\t}\n  1061\t\t\t\t} else {\n  1062\t\t\t\t\t// Log at least once at high value, then debug. Otherwise it gets very verbose.\n  1063\t\t\t\t\tif diff <= 3*leaseTimeout {\n  1064\t\t\t\t\t\tr.logger.Warn(\"failed to contact\", \"server-id\", server.ID, \"time\", diff)\n  1065\t\t\t\t\t} else {\n  1066\t\t\t\t\t\tr.logger.Debug(\"failed to contact\", \"server-id\", server.ID, \"time\", diff)\n  1067\t\t\t\t\t}\n  1068\t\t\t\t}\n  1069\t\t\t\tmetrics.AddSample([]string{\"raft\", \"leader\", \"lastContact\"}, float32(diff/time.Millisecond))\n  1070\t\t\t}\n  1071\t\t}\n  1072\t\n  1073\t\t// Verify we can contact a quorum\n  1074\t\tquorum := r.quorumSize()\n  1075\t\tif contacted < quorum {\n  1076\t\t\tr.logger.Warn(\"failed to contact quorum of nodes, stepping down\")\n  1077\t\t\tr.setState(Follower)\n  1078\t\t\tmetrics.IncrCounter([]string{\"raft\", \"transition\", \"leader_lease_timeout\"}, 1)\n  1079\t\t}\n  1080\t\treturn maxDiff\n  1081\t}\n  1082\t\n  1083\t// quorumSize is used to return the quorum size. This must only be called on\n  1084\t// the main thread.\n  1085\t// TODO: revisit usage\n  1086\tfunc (r *Raft) quorumSize() int {\n  1087\t\tvoters := 0\n  1088\t\tfor _, server := range r.configurations.latest.Servers {\n  1089\t\t\tif server.Suffrage == Voter {\n  1090\t\t\t\tvoters++\n  1091\t\t\t}\n  1092\t\t}\n  1093\t\treturn voters/2 + 1\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"The trusted run recorded both completed histories. With nonvoter connectivity, the old term-2 leader returned successful verification after the term-3 replacement completed its write; without that connectivity, verification failed on lease-driven step-down. The saved oracle matches the public API promise. The documentation also describes verification as contacting voters. Exact vote-edge attribution and uniform-timeout behavior remain outside this result.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > build_review.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nartifact='318065aead82494797d283e378195a4e'\nexecution='bcaed4ce26bf44d797a18ec78b37a154'\nsources=[{'id':'S-doc-verify-voters','file':'docs/README.md','start_line':38,'end_line':49,'kind':'document_statement'},{'id':'S-verify-future-purpose','file':'future.go','start_line':236,'end_line':244,'kind':'interface_statement'},{'id':'S-read-leader-contract','file':'README.md','start_line':68,'end_line':77,'kind':'document_statement'}]\nitems=[\n {'aspect':'applicability','status':'no_issue_found','source_ids':['S-api-verify','S-doc-verify-voters','S-verify-future-purpose','S-read-leader-contract','S-membership-contract','S-control-config','S-control-config-validation','S-verify-existing-tests'],\n 'rationale':'Reviewed O-verify-current-authority version 1 selected by artifact 318065aead82494797d283e378195a4e, not a proposed stronger voter-count rule. S-api-verify explicitly promises assurance that this peer is still leader for preventing stale FSM reads; S-verify-future-purpose gives the same purpose. S-doc-verify-voters describes heartbeat confirmation from voters, consistent with S-membership-contract restricting election participation. In the actual fixed history a different peer completes a command in a higher term before the call, so the old success cannot be ordered before that authority change. A weaker guarantee of merely returning the local role would not satisfy this API purpose. S-control-config and S-control-config-validation define and validate local timing parameters without imposing cross-node equality; the scoped heterogeneous settings are actual NewRaft inputs, not direct timer/role mutations. The lease is a protective mechanism, not a documented exception to VerifyLeader assurance before its expiry. The tests in S-verify-existing-tests cover narrower healthy and known-loss cases and do not excuse success after an independently established replacement election.',\n 'counterevidence':[],\n 'limitations':['This interpretation concerns the public leadership assurance, not a full read-linearizability theorem or invalid log commitment.','The executed deployment is crash-free protocol v3 with fixed membership and nonuniform timeouts; uniform timers and arbitrary deployment configurations were not executed.']},\n {'aspect':'decomposition','status':'no_issue_found','source_ids':['S-api-verify','S-election','S-vote-producer','S-repl-membership','S-verify-register','S-notify','S-verify-vote','S-leader-loop','S-lease','S-leader-session','S-commitment'],\n 'rationale':'The obligation expresses a necessary condition for a successful authority assurance, specialized to independently observed prior replacement leadership. It permits failure or pending work; it does not equate support availability with required success. Actual election workers establish the replacement context, and a successful Apply future plus FSM value supplies its subsequent completed operation. The verification path is separate: all replication workers are registered (S-repl-membership/S-verify-register), detached notifications supply booleans (S-notify), and the scalar threshold is consumed into a nil response (S-verify-vote/S-leader-loop). Existing alternatives were retained: received higher-term replies, a negative verification vote, voter-only lease expiry and tenure cleanup can reject old authority. The partition prevents majority replies by the configured fault, while all local workers run. The control reaches the lease/cleanup alternative and fails verification. Commitment remains voter-filtered (S-commitment), so this observation does not imply log-safety failure. Even if this conditional obligation always held, other stale-read histories could remain, including leadership changes during the invocation and un-applied earlier commands; this is deliberately not a sufficient decomposition of all read safety.',\n 'counterevidence':[],\n 'limitations':['No instrument observes the exact notifyAll-to-vote edge for this future. Source, fresh nonvoter response counters and the independent connectivity control support the cause hypothesis but do not uniquely exclude a pre-partition voter response whose consumption was delayed.','The control is a separate complete history. It is not used as an earlier or later segment of the violating history.']},\n {'aspect':'checker_correspondence','status':'no_issue_found','source_ids':['S-api-verify','S-future-error','S-future-completion','S-bootstrap','S-startup','S-membership-api','S-config-dispatch','S-control-transport','S-control-config-validation','S-replicate','S-election','S-vote-producer','S-api-apply','S-fsm-worker','S-mock-fsm','S-observation-api','S-config-observation','S-verify-register','S-verify-vote','S-leader-loop','S-lease','S-leader-session'],\n 'rationale':'Inspected the saved plan.json and assurance_generated_test.go under direct-checks/f0fd7479adcd418884ccfb446842e310, bindings L-verify-api/L-verify-registration/L-verify-count/L-verify-completion version 1, raw stdout/stderr for execution bcaed4ce26bf44d797a18ec78b37a154, and its monitor_results. The constructor alone is not treated as the prefix: the harness executes BootstrapCluster, timer-driven single-voter election, successful sequential membership futures, an initial successful Apply, all-node FSM/CommitIndex checks and membership-content checks. No term, role, vote, commitment or FSM state is assigned. It cuts both directions between {old,nonvoter} and the other voters, then observes the actual replacement State/CurrentTerm and successfully completed Apply before verification. Pipeline support is declined through the existing fallback; ordinary RPC bodies and responses are real and unmodified. MockFSM reads are mutex-protected; the result is not inferred from AppliedIndex. The only static true success field, replacement_write.write_ok, is emitted after the actual Apply Error has returned nil, otherwise t.Fatal exits. The result ok field is computed from the actual VerifyLeader future Error.\\\\n\\\\nThe monitor admits alias invoked, whose new_id reference requires replacement to precede it. Unique op values occur in replacement_write, verify_invocation and verify_result; mutable term/role and the tested ok value are not identity filters. The trigger selects verify_result and the oracle compares ok==false, independently of the driver. Raw events 3/4/5 form one complete witness: with_nonvoter_node_2 is elected in term 3 and completes index 8 with value after; old node_0 remains term 2 with value before and invokes verification at partition elapsed 245ms; its actual future returns nil with ok=true at 245ms. New leader remains Leader term 3. The nonvoter successful-response count rises 32 to 33, while voter counts remain 5 and 3. Events 9/10/11 form the separate control: a real term-3 successor completes index 8 before old invocation; old verification returns leadership-lost with ok=false and Follower state at 2008ms. Both healthy setup verifications return nil. The observed antecedent is therefore nonvacuous, both admitted operations complete, and no timeout is interpreted as a property result.\\\\n\\\\nThe runner reports completed execution, exit 0, no changed target files and no parsing errors. The exit status shows the observation driver completed, not that the property held: the external comparison marks event 5 violated and event 11 permitted, with no missing identities or correlations. Shutdown is initiated only after actual result emission and does not produce the measured error. These observations correspond to the obligation\\\\'s public endpoint in its fixed scope. This review does not independently prove the original nonvoter-cause hypothesis or extend the result to production reads, arbitrary timing, or consensus log disagreement.',\n 'counterevidence':[],\n 'limitations':['The driver uses polling and real randomized elections; this is one observed finite execution, not exhaustive scheduling.','No caller-facing read service is executed; before/after are direct observations of the repository MockFSM.','No network fast-path, pipeline, crash/restart, concurrent reconfiguration or uniform-timeout case is covered.']}\n]\nsub={'action':'review','artifact_id':artifact,'rationale':'Review the fixed direct artifact and its actual trusted execution as a whole; retain the complete public API witness while separating cause and broader consequences.','sources':sources,'review_items':items,'resolutions':[],\n 'feedback':{'ref_ids':[artifact,execution,'O-verify-current-authority','S-api-verify','S-doc-verify-voters','S-lease','S-commitment','S-term-persist','S-vote-handler'],\n 'answered':'Trusted execution bcaed4ce26bf44d797a18ec78b37a154 supplies a complete public VerifyLeader discrepancy in the accepted fixed scope: a term-3 replacement completed a write before a term-2 old leader returned successful verification while its FSM retained the prior value. The independent no-nonvoter-contact history completes with leadership-loss failure, preserving the lease protection. This review found no correspondence or applicability issue in the fixed public-endpoint comparison; result attribution is for the controller to record. Newly read documentation describes verification as contacting voters and agrees with the existing public assurance. The original exact-support cause remains narrower evidence than the completed public discrepancy.',\n 'remaining':['Exact per-future nonvoter vote attribution and uniform-timeout behavior remain unexecuted; neither is required to erase or establish the observed fixed-scope API comparison.','Other mapped consensus relationships and deferred surfaces remain unchecked, particularly persistence failures and concurrent heartbeat/context updates.'],\n 'understanding':'unchanged',\n 'rationale':'Return to the frontier after this local result. Further nonvoter vote instrumen